# global-out-put: Does `out_put=1` in a global action list add an output row at the crossing (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: t@3=0.55 rows=6
# pc: ok
# ruling: pc-ode accepts `arret` and `out_put` as undeclared global targets. The model is simulation only, so pc-ir refuses it with SimulationOnly (language.md, Statement details). `nout` is read as `njmp` (without it the run writes 21 rows), so the parse has no diagnostic.
x'=1
x(0)=0
aux v=x
global 1 x-0.55 {out_put=1}
@ total=2,dt=0.1,meth=euler,nout=5
